I edited prompt text in four places in `out/main-A.workflow.json`, all in the opening, identity and negotiate steps. Transitions, the start code node and the account post-processing code are untouched, and the file loads with python3 (6 nodes). I did not save to Freya or run any eval or chat, so none of these fixes has been tested yet. All failures were real requirements of the brief, so I ignored none.

- **Job loss + payment-plan request (d1df0c33), wrong queue and close reason:** fixed. Rule 32 says hardship comes before rule 41, so the persona check is right. The negotiate step now says that if illness, a death in the family or job loss comes up, even in the same turn as asking for a plan, the agent offers support, transfers to queue `support` and closes `transferred` / `support`. The plan-request rule now applies only when no hardship was mentioned.
- **Three wrong answers (6e2a3522), `verify_identity` refused with "identity check is over" on 6632:** fixed. Four checks were sent for three answers, so one answer was apparently checked twice. The transcript doesn't show the call arguments, so that cause is inferred. The agent also moved on to the phone question after the wrong date of birth instead of asking it again. The identity step now says: check each new answer exactly once, never resend an answer, ask the same question again after a wrong answer, and read `wrong_answers_left`. Once that is 0 or the check is over, it never calls `verify_identity` again; it says the mobile app / branch line and closes `not_verified` / `failed` (rules 12 and 14).
- **Three wrong answers (b030a172), refused when checking the corrected 1992-07-21 after the check was over:** fixed by the same identity edit. Any correction offered after the check has ended is not sent; the agent closes `not_verified` / `failed`.
- **Relative and callback time (a4a4ddae), no callback scheduled and closed `no_callback`:** fixed. The sister's second time, Thursday 15 October at 18:30, is the next business day after 14 October and inside 10:00–19:00, so rule 6 required scheduling it. The opening step now says to convert the day and time to YYYY-MM-DD and HH:MM ("half past six in the evening" = 18:30). A day counts as allowed if it is on the CALLBACK line in DATE FACTS, a corrected time is checked again from scratch, and the agent must call `schedule_callback` in that same turn instead of saying "one moment". It then closes `not_reached` / `callback`.

